      "summary": "King Solomon loves many strange women — the daughter of Pharaoh, Moabites, Ammonites, Edomites, Zidonians, and Hittites — from the very nations God had warned would turn Israel's heart. He has seven hundred wives and three hundred concubines, and when he is old his wives turn his heart after other gods: Ashtoreth of the Zidonians, Milcom and Molech of the Ammonites, Chemosh of Moab, for whom he builds high places on the hill before Jerusalem. The Lord is angry with him, for He had appeared to him twice, and declares that the kingdom will be torn from him — though not in his days, for David's sake, and one tribe will remain for his son. God raises up adversaries: Hadad the Edomite, who had fled to Egypt as a child when Joab slaughtered Edom's males and married into Pharaoh's family, and Rezon, a rebel who seizes Damascus and abhors Israel. Most dangerously, Solomon's own able taskmaster Jeroboam meets the prophet Ahijah of Shiloh on the road; Ahijah tears his new garment into twelve pieces and gives Jeroboam ten, promising him a lasting house if he will obey. Solomon seeks to kill Jeroboam, who flees to Shishak in Egypt, and after forty years' reign Solomon sleeps with his fathers and Rehoboam his son reigns in his stead.",
