      "summary": "All Israel gathers at Shechem to crown Solomon's son Rehoboam, and Jeroboam, back from exile in Egypt, leads them in a simple request: lighten the grievous yoke your father laid on us, and we will serve you. The old men who stood before Solomon counsel gentleness; the young men who grew up with Rehoboam tell him to boast that his little finger will be thicker than his father's loins, and to promise scorpions where Solomon used whips. Rehoboam takes the young men's advice, and the northern tribes answer with the old cry of revolt: 'What portion have we in David? to your tents, O Israel.' They stone Adoram, the officer over the forced labor, and Rehoboam flees in his chariot to Jerusalem. The prophet Shemaiah forbids Judah to march north, for 'this thing is from me,' and the tribes obey. Jeroboam, fearing that pilgrimages to the Temple will pull hearts back to David's house, sets up two golden calves at Bethel and Dan, appoints non-Levite priests, and invents a feast in the eighth month 'which he had devised of his own heart.'",
