      "summary": "As Jeroboam stands at his new altar in Bethel to burn incense, a man of God from Judah cries out against the altar itself: a son of David named Josiah will one day burn the bones of its priests upon it. When Jeroboam stretches out his hand and orders him seized, the hand dries up so he cannot draw it back, and the altar splits and pours out its ashes, just as the prophet said. At the man of God's prayer the king's hand is restored, but he refuses Jeroboam's invitation to dine, for the Lord has commanded him to eat no bread, drink no water, and go home by another way. Then an old prophet of Bethel rides after him, finds him resting under an oak, and lies to him — an angel told me to bring you home. The man of God eats at his table, and in the middle of the meal the old prophet himself pronounces his doom. On the road a lion kills him but does not eat him or the donkey, standing beside the body in eerie stillness; the old prophet buries him in his own grave, mourns 'Alas, my brother,' and asks to be buried beside him. And still Jeroboam does not turn from his evil way.",
