      "summary": "Rehoboam's son Abijam reigns three short years in Jerusalem, walking in his father's sins, yet the Lord keeps a lamp burning in Jerusalem 'for David's sake.' His son Asa, however, rules forty-one years and does what is right like David: he drives out the cult prostitutes, removes the idols, and even deposes his own grandmother Maachah as queen mother, cutting down her obscene Asherah image and burning it by the brook Kidron. When Baasha of Israel fortifies Ramah to choke off traffic into Jerusalem, Asa strips the Temple treasury and bribes Ben-hadad of Damascus to break his treaty with Israel; the Arameans ravage Israel's northern towns, Baasha withdraws, and Asa's men haul away Ramah's stones to build Geba and Mizpah. In the north, Jeroboam's son Nadab reigns barely two years before Baasha assassinates him during the siege of Gibbethon and wipes out Jeroboam's entire house, exactly as Ahijah had foretold. Yet Baasha walks in Jeroboam's way, and the war between the two kings continues all their days.",
