      "num": 17,
      "title": "Elijah, the Ravens, and the Widow's Jar",
      "summary": "Out of nowhere, Elijah the Tishbite from Gilead stands before Ahab and declares that there will be neither dew nor rain these years except by his word. God sends him to hide by the brook Cherith east of the Jordan, where ravens bring him bread and meat morning and evening, until the brook itself dries up. Then God sends him into Baal's home territory, to Zarephath near Sidon, where a widow gathering sticks is preparing a last meal of flour and oil for herself and her son before they die. Elijah asks her to make him a cake first, promising that the barrel of meal will not waste nor the cruse of oil fail until the rain returns — and it happens day after day. Later her son falls sick and stops breathing, and in her grief she accuses the prophet of coming to remind God of her sin. Elijah carries the boy to the upper room, stretches himself on him three times, and cries to the Lord, and the child's soul comes back into him. The widow confesses: now I know that you are a man of God and that the Lord's word in your mouth is truth.",
