      "summary": "Naboth of Jezreel owns a vineyard next to Ahab's palace, and Ahab wants it for a vegetable garden, offering a better vineyard or its price in money. Naboth refuses: 'The LORD forbid it me, that I should give the inheritance of my fathers unto thee.' Ahab goes home sullen, lies on his bed with his face to the wall, and will not eat. Jezebel mocks him — 'Dost thou now govern the kingdom of Israel?' — and writes letters in Ahab's name, sealed with his seal, ordering the elders of Jezreel to proclaim a fast, seat Naboth prominently, and have two worthless men accuse him of cursing God and the king. The elders obey; Naboth is stoned outside the city, and Ahab rises to take possession. There Elijah meets him with the word of the Lord: in the place where dogs licked Naboth's blood they will lick yours, and dogs will eat Jezebel by the wall of Jezreel. Ahab tears his clothes, puts on sackcloth, fasts, and goes softly — and God tells Elijah that because Ahab has humbled himself, the disaster will come in his son's days instead.",
